"Peace of mind is a minor wordchain taught at Artonan consulates."
"It calms the mind for about three hours."
"Its blowback, a quiet but anxious mind, lasts about as long."
"Beginners need a few dozen tries before a first success."
"It begins: 'My heart calls out to another in good faith.'"
"It asks: 'Spare me a portion of your mind's ease in this hour when my own mind is troubled.'"
"It promises: 'Tomorrow, I will grant another an equal comfort of mind.'"
"Two backlashes within a few hours can flatten the chanter."
"Its sacrifice half brings fear and dread, the opposite of peace of mind."
